-- title:
--   Degeneracy pull-backs lie in the K-node ring, residues reduced
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q$, a valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ (an algebraic closure of $\mathbb Q$), a nonzero level $N$, an algebraically closed field $k$ of characteristic $q$ and a ring homomorphism $\mathrm{red} : A \to k$; fix modular polynomial data `data` for $q$ satisfying the Kronecker congruence `hKr`, integrality hypotheses $h\alpha$, $h\beta$ for the two level-raising maps $\alpha =$ `heckeAlphaBar` (the inclusion of the level-$N$ field into the level-$Nq$ field) and $\beta =$ `heckeBetaBar` (the same inclusion composed with $\mathfrak q \mapsto \mathfrak q^{q}$), a place specialisation $P$ of these data, and a prolongation tuple $R$ over $P$. Assume $q \nmid N$. Let $K$ be a finite extension of $\mathbb Q$ inside $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, and let $w$ be a place of the level-$N$ geometric function field $k(j, j_N)$ over $k$ lying in `ssPlaces q N k`, i.e. $w$ is rational, is an affine geometric place, and its value at the geometric $j$-generator is a supersingular $j$-invariant for $q$. Let $y$ be a Laurent series with coefficients in the subring $A \cap K$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, and let $g$ belong to $\overline{\mathbb Q} \cdot \mathbb Q(X_{\mathrm{full}}(N))$, the $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-subfield of $\overline{\mathbb Q}((\mathfrak q))$ generated by the coefficientwise images of the full level-$N$ expansions, such that: the expansion of $g$ is the coefficientwise image of $y$ under $A \cap K \hookrightarrow \overline{\mathbb Q}$; $g$ lies in the subfield of $\overline{\mathbb Q}((\mathfrak q))$ generated by the constant series from the integers of $K$ together with $j$ and $j_N$; and $g$ is integral over the $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-subalgebra generated by the expansions of $j$ and of $j_N$. Then both $\alpha(g)$ and $\beta(g)$ lie in `R.nodeIntegersOver K w`, that is, each lies in the integers of both regular prolongations $R_1$, $R_2$ and in the valuation subring of every place $V$ of the level-$Nq$ field with $P.\mathrm{reduceFst}\,V = w$, and its expansion lies in the corresponding subfield attached to $K$ at level $Nq$; moreover the residue `R.nodeResidue₁ w` of $\alpha(g)$ and the residue `R.nodeResidue₂ w` of $\beta(g)$, read as Laurent series over $k$, both equal the coefficientwise reduction of $y$ under $A \cap K \to k$ induced by $\mathrm{red}$.
--
--   This is the integrality statement for the two degeneracy pull-backs to level $Nq$ of a level-$N$ modular function whose $\mathfrak q$-expansion has coefficients in $A \cap K$ and which is integral over $\overline{\mathbb Q}[j, j_N]$: both pull-backs are integral at the supersingular node attached to $w$, with residue the coefficientwise reduction of the expansion. It feeds the construction of uniformisers and the saturation properties of the node residue maps used in the study of the reduction of $X_0(Nq)$ at $q$.
